From: slice78 <audit@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0012] slice 78: the read ledger records itself

Slice 77 built reserved_holdout and seeded it BY HAND. That caught the
slice-57 contamination retroactively, which is worth something, but a ledger
maintained by hand is a good intention. Good intentions are exactly what
failed in slice 57: every procedural guard passed, and nobody checked whether
the bytes had been read before.

market_data.load_corpus is the chokepoint every measurement tool routes
through. That is where recording belongs.

 ~ market_data.py       READ_OBSERVER = None, called after every successful
                        corpus load with (symbol, first_ms, last_ms).
                        NO NEW IMPORTS. INTEGRATION_MAP §1 says dependencies
                        point downward and test_the_module_imports_only_
                        stdlib_numpy_and_config enforces it, so market_data
                        knows nothing about the ledger - it publishes raw
                        epoch-ms and the ledger reaches UP to observe.
                        Raw ms because formatting would need datetime, which
                        is not on this module's allowlist either.

 ~ tools/reserved_holdout.py   + install() sets the observer
                        + auto_record(): IDEMPOTENT (a re-run is not a second
                          look) and NEVER FATAL (an unwritable artifacts/ must
                          not kill a measurement at its last line - slice 77
                          fixed that failure mode once already)
                        + LEDGER_DISABLED kill switch

 ~ tools/*.py (28)      every non-archival tool that calls load_corpus now
                        installs the ledger first. The 16 digest-pinned
                        historical slice tools are UNTOUCHED: they are
                        provenance records, and rewriting them would
                        retroactively falsify how past measurements were made.

 + tests/conftest.py    LEDGER_DISABLED=1 for the session. The suite loads
                        corpora hundreds of times and none of those looks
                        informed a hypothesis; left unsuppressed they would
                        bury the six reads that matter.

 + tests/test_slice78_ledger_is_automatic.py   16 tests. The load-bearing one
                        scans tools/ and FAILS THE BUILD if a corpus reader
                        does not install the ledger - the same idiom as the
                        AST test that forbids assigning live_authorized. It
                        does not ask anyone to be careful.

TWO GUARDS CAUGHT ME AND BOTH WERE RIGHT:
  test_the_module_imports_only_stdlib_numpy_and_config rejected importing the
  ledger into market_data. Rebuilt as an observer; arrow still points down.
  test_no_handler_silently_passes rejected `except: pass` in the install
  snippet - "an exception swallowed without a word is a failure nobody will
  ever see". The reason is now bound and the flag legible.

NOT TOUCHED: FUND_ABS, the join, HORIZON, the barrier, the folds, the caps,
the schedule, GATE_PATH, live_authorized, Stage-1 artefacts, project_status.
The slice-77 freeze note remains UNSIGNED.

VERIFIED: 5,066 passed, 2 skipped (was 5,057). Ladder still 5/4/0/0/0/0.
Ledger unchanged by a full test run.

